<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="012" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Per-table rules registry replacing five column lists (FR-11)</title>
    <phase>2 W2 Unified RecordCreationService</phase>
    <gate>010 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api; tags include bff-api and refactor; adds an ArchTest and unit tests at KEEP paths (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Consolidates five lists whose per-table differences encode ownership and protection policy; must preserve each difference deliberately and record rationale.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W2-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>010</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, dataverse, refactor, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Create one declarative per-table rules registry, `Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs`, holding for each create table: root or child; protected columns; autonumber column; "for"-person column; server defaults; search-indexed Y/N; mapping-applies Y/N; and any ownership exception with its rationale. It replaces `MatterProtectedAttributes` / `ProjectProtectedAttributes` (Office `RecordCreationService`), `ServerOwnedColumns` and `ForPersonColumns` (`OwnedChildWrite`) and `RootServerOwnedColumns` (`ChildRecordEndpoints`). Keep the old lists' consumers compiling (the lists may become views over the registry) until tasks 013 and 018 switch consumers over. Add an arch test that fails when a create table lacks a registry entry.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse write-path invariants. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>One registry is the single source for per-table create rules; every existing create table has an entry derived from the current lists with no behaviour change; an arch test (with a negative control) fails when a create table has no entry.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-11, Placement table row "Per-table rules registry"; design.md §4. Today five lists define protection and ownership per core and already differ: `MatterProtectedAttributes` ~:249 and `ProjectProtectedAttributes` ~:264 in Services/Office/RecordCreationService.cs; `ServerOwnedColumns` ~:64 and `ForPersonColumns` ~:186 in Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs; `RootServerOwnedColumns` ~:84 in Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs (with `CreateTables` ~:66). Consumers include ChildRecordEndpoints (~:250, ~:490), DataverseCreateRecordHandler (~:496 uses ForPersonColumns), SignalReadService (documents ForPersonColumns) and the Office Matter/Project create paths. The registry is data plus lookups; the consuming switch-over is in tasks 013 (service), 014 and 018 (Office adapter). Re-grep every reference before editing.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs (~:64 ServerOwnedColumns, ~:186 ForPersonColumns become views over the registry; same public shape)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs (~:84 RootServerOwnedColumns and ~:66 CreateTables become views over the registry; same behaviour)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/RecordCreationService.cs (~:249, ~:264 the two protected lists become views over the registry)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRulesTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordTableRulesRegistryGuardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (census guard style; source-scan precedent and baseline/ratchet shape)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs (~:496 consumer of ForPersonColumns; read only)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="required">Coordination gate: OwnedChildWrite.cs is shared with UAC-r2; confirm sequencing in notes/decisions.md.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: behaviour. The registry is derived from today's lists; for every table the effective protected, server-owned and for-person sets after this task equal the union/differences that exist today (the existing per-core differences are preserved as explicit per-table entries, not merged away). Any value that looks wrong is recorded in the task notes and left as is.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. The registry is a static declarative type; no DI registration, no interface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: invariants. Each ownership exception is a named registry rule with a rationale string; the registry declares policy, it does not enforce it (the service does, task 013).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added by this task. Unit tests under `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` and the guard under `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/`; every guard has a must-fire and a must-not-fire control; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`; no DI-registration tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. State Placement Justification in the PR; measure publish-size delta against a fresh master build per root CLAUDE.md §10.4; run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Per-table create rules; write-path invariants</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/data.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="entity-operations" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/entity-operations.md">Column and table naming.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; read spec FR-11 and the Placement table; confirm task 010 sign-off; run /conflict-check; re-grep all five lists and every consumer.</step>
    <step order="1">Inventory: build a table (task notes) of every create table (CreateTables plus Matter, Project, Invoice and any table named in ForPersonColumns) against the five lists, showing which list contains which column per table.</step>
    <step order="2">Define the registry type: per table, root/child; protected columns; autonumber column; for-person column; server defaults; search-indexed Y/N; mapping-applies Y/N; ownership exception (name plus rationale). Populate it from the inventory; use "grep for X" evidence in comments only where a value is not visible in the old lists, and mark such values for owner review rather than inventing them.</step>
    <step order="3">Re-express the old lists as views over the registry (same member names and types) so consumers compile unchanged; run all existing tests.</step>
    <step order="4">Unit tests: for every table, the view equals the pre-change list content (snapshot taken from the inventory); lookup of a table with no entry returns not-found.</step>
    <step order="5">Arch guard: every table in `CreateTables` (and every table the unified service will accept) has a registry entry; include a must-fire control (a fixture table with no entry makes the guard fail) and a must-not-fire control (all entries present passes).</step>
    <step order="6">Build + run tests; measure publish size; run the CVE check.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If two cores disagree about the same table's protected columns in a way that changes security (one allows what the other forbids), record both as separate named entries, STOP, and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 instead of choosing the stricter or looser one.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grep for `MatterProtectedAttributes`, `ProjectProtectedAttributes`, `ServerOwnedColumns`, `RootServerOwnedColumns` and `ForPersonColumns` finds five separate lists in three files (Services/Office/RecordCreationService.cs, Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs, Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs); no registry exists (grep for `RecordTableRules` returns nothing).</existing>
    <extension>This consolidates the five lists into one (spec §11 row "Per-table rules registry": Yes, consolidates five lists). A new file is needed because the lists live in three different cores that cannot reference each other, and the new Services/RecordCreation/ folder is the unified service's home.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Protected and server-owned columns keep drifting between create paths (they already differ per core), and the unified service (task 013) has no single place to read per-table policy, search-index and mapping applicability.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools><tool name="dotnet">Build/test .NET</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRulesTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordTableRulesRegistryGuardTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`RecordTableRules` holds, per table: root/child, protected columns, autonumber column, for-person column, server defaults, search-indexed Y/N, mapping-applies Y/N, and any ownership exception with a non-empty rationale.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The five old lists are views over the registry (no independent column literals remain in them); a unit test per table proves each view equals the pre-change content recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The arch guard fails when a create table lacks a registry entry (must-fire control) and passes when all are present (must-not-fire control).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no consumer's observable behaviour changed — existing tests for ChildRecordEndpoints, DataverseCreateRecordHandler, OwnedChildWrite and the Office quick-create pass unchanged; no ownership exception lacks a rationale.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; full BFF unit tests and ArchTests pass; publish-size delta and CVE result recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-11. The old lists are deleted (not just viewed) when tasks 013, 014 and 018 switch their consumers; that final deletion is acceptance-checked there. Search-indexed and mapping-applies flags are consumed by tasks 014 and 015.
Completed 2026-10-20 (task/fm-012 @ 69b3a33047, merged with master to 77ef24010e). RecordTableRules registry (17 tables); the five per-table lists now read from it with no behaviour change; registry guard ArchTest with must-fire and must-not-fire controls; the ebilling invoice-family rule shape and the ontology OntologyContentIsNotMapped exclusion are expressible. Merged verify: Spaarke.sln 0/0, ArchTests 1183/1183, suites 1746 pass. Publish +4,903 B cumulative vs fresh master; no CVE. Details and the ebilling reconciliation recipe: notes/task-012-notes.md.
rework: fix-round-1 task 012</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
